Steps to add a new language
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

dil.nsi: add the following lines (each in appropiate place):

  !include l10n/templates/en.nsh

  ; LANG_MYLANGUAGE must be a valid string recognised by Nsis.  If your
  ; language is not yet supported by Nsis, please translate the missing
  ; Nsis part first.
  Push ${LANG_MYLANGUAGE}
  Push Mylanguage

l10n/generate_template.sh: tell the script how to identify the charset that
is used on Windows.

  case $LANGUAGE in
    blah)
  	charset=my_windows_charset ;;
    *)	charset=utf-8 ;;
  esac

l10n/po/: write your .po file as usual.

l10n/Makefile: add your language to LINGUAS variable.
